      "id": "q3-robot",
      "track": "section-b",
      "title": "Section B, Question 3",
      "markdown": "There is a robot which walks and paints the ground at the same time. It accepts 3 kinds of command only:\n\n- F: Go forward by 1 unit\n- T: Turn right by 90 degrees\n- n(commands): Repeat commands n times, where 0 ≤ n ≤ 9\n\n“@” is the position where the robot starts. The robot is facing upward when starts.\n\n4(FT) does the same thing using the repeat command. Although both commands give the same result, we prefer the later one as it is shorter. Beware that each open/close bracket is counted as a character."
    }
  ],
